<%--
Raw_Text_Input

Edits a Raw_Text value - a block of user-authored PLAIN text.

$placeholder - Placeholder text
$rows        - Textarea rows (default 4)
$seeder      - Seeder function name for test data

Widget interface:
- val() - Get/set a Raw_Text INSTANCE (never a string)

This is deliberately a SEPARATE component from Text_Input rather than a mode of it.
An input component edits exactly one kind of value, which is what lets ACCEPTS refuse
a mismatch: Text_Input edits varchar strings, Raw_Text_Input edits Raw_Text, and neither
can be pointed at the other's column by accident. A TEXT column is not a long varchar -
it holds a block of authored content whose encoding the model declares, and the editor
for it is chosen by that declaration.

Usage:
<Raw_Text_Input $name="notes" $rows=4 $placeholder="Internal notes..." />
--%>
<Define:Raw_Text_Input extends="Form_Input_Abstract">
    <textarea $sid="input"
              class="form-control"
              rows="<%= this.args.rows || 4 %>"
              placeholder="<%= this.args.placeholder || '' %>"
              <% if (this.args.disabled) { %>disabled<% } %>></textarea>
</Define:Raw_Text_Input>
